 @dragonking2849  "Why not just make more of the other more value proportionate 3000 series if they have enough chips to go around."

They have excess of 3090's die, not 3080's. They are short on VRAM and hence the 3080ti that's actually a 3090 with half the VRAM. The Fabs that produce wafers for GPUs are bought/reserved from at least 6 months ago and there is no space left. This is a case of excess 3090 die due to shortage of VRAM. It's not a case of "enough chips to go around". 

They don't grab a chip from the back and write "3090" on it.

